      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It’s understandable that you see rebuilding as a hollow effort when the loss feels so total—your identity, your influence, the respect you once commanded. Still, even small, authentic steps—like setting a single, manageable goal each day or reconnecting with one person who still sees your value—can slowly begin to repair the foundation instead of just covering cracks. Remember, you don’t have to “pretend”; you can acknowledge the brokenness while still allowing room for growth, and professional support can help you navigate that space without having to shoulder it alone.",
